🔒 CORE MUSICAL CONSTRAINTS (LOCKED)
Tempo: ~128–132 BPM (light, buoyant, never rushed)
Meter: 4/4 with subtle internal syncopation (feels like skipping steps)
Key center: bright major tonality with modal color (Lydian-leaning lift via raised 4th)
Harmony: simple, diatonic progressions with gentle suspensions; no heavy blues tension
Dynamics: soft → warm → slightly fuller → back to soft (no big climax)

🎸 INSTRUMENTATION (WEIGHTED)
Primary guitar: clean acoustic steel-string, capoed high on the neck
light fingerpicking + soft strums
percussive taps on the guitar body (human, intimate)
Secondary texture: subtle electric guitar harmonics or doubled acoustic shimmer
Percussion:
brushed drums or light hand percussion
taps, shakers, gentle kick — never a heavy backbeat
Bass: melodic, supportive, walking lightly — felt more than heard
Optional color: faint strings or Moog-like warmth, blended low

🎤 VOCAL CONSTRAINTS
Lead vocal: warm, relaxed male tenor
close-mic’d, intimate, smiling through the phrasing
no grit, no aggression, no belting

Backing vocals:
soft stacked harmonies
enter only in later sections, like sunlight filling the room
never dominate the lead

🌞 MELODIC & RHYTHMIC CHARACTER
Melody rises gently, often stepping upward (hopeful contour)
